{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501036-could-a-technofetish-be-upgraded","id":1501036,"title":"Could a technofetish be \"upgraded?\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-22T08:52:49-08:00","id":1501036,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Could a technofetish be \"upgraded?\"","content":"One of my game's PCs (GW Ragabash) has a fetish called a &quot;TPS&quot; or Tellurian Positioning System. It allows him to, with enough information and time, track a single spirit unerringly.<br /> He loves it and uses it with some frequency.<br /> As he gains ranks, we were considering the idea that he could, both technologically and spiritually, tinker with it; upgrading functionality. <br /> Obviously this might involve some additional spirit negotiations and chiminage. Maybe a quest or 2.<br /> Any thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27674-johnnyarkham","name":"JohnnyArkham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T10:44:38-08:00","id":1501040,"title":"","content":"The whole idea of the Fetish is that you have agreed with the spirit to do this one thing in this specially constructed temple to its own power. However, I think it might be viable to undertake the rites to get the spirit inside to stop being dormant and speak to you, and you could offer it greater commitments and a greater &quot;temple&quot; for just a bit more of its power. This would likely require you to build another device and perform the rite of the fetish, and the spirit would most likely be well inclined towards it if it was used in the correct way and treated with respect.<br /> <br /> The act of just upgrading the device of the techno spirit would usually just be maintenance, rather than changing its essence and would be a part of your duty to the spirit, the device itself might gain additional functionality, but the fetish would stay the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T13:31:02-08:00","id":1501051,"title":"","content":"I would say no, but there isn't a problem to create a second fetish that has the upgraded capabilities. Maybe even the Garou can destroy the existing fetish to release the spirit and ask the same spirit if he wants to inhabit a new one and provide greater powers.<br /> <br /> If you allow one fetish to be upgraded, then it becomes an issue of why can't other fetishes be upgraded, or even all of them? And if that is possible, then why hasn't it already been done and become a normal thing to do? What does it mean that the original agreement negotiated between the spirit and fetish maker can be subsequently changed? What kind of impact does that have? I think such a thing opens up a lot of questions about the nature of fetishes, agreements with spirits, etc. that could make problems for you as an ST down the way since you'll need to come up with answers for questions that don't currently exist.<br /> <br /> Just my initial thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T08:19:53-08:00","id":1501235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501036-could-a-technofetish-be-upgraded?p=1501040#post1501040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">to get the spirit inside to stop being dormant and speak to you</div> </div> </div> </div>Is dormancy of spirits in fetishes RAW? I never played it like that- on the contrary, I treat fetish-bound spirits as pretty awake and in need of continued (albeit minor) chiminage. The moment a player treats a fetish like a mere object, the spirit would get annoyed. For example, the player with a Magpie's Swag regularly puts small glittery baubles into it for the spirit.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, I agree with the others. Upgrading a fetish would mean to craft a new one and offer it to the spirit as a new home. That came up once in my sessions, when the player was interested in developing one of the fetish spirits alongside her character. We ended up making the spirit her familiar, and I plundered Mage rules for advancement and powers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T09:35:19-08:00","id":1501242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1501036-could-a-technofetish-be-upgraded?p=1501235#post1501235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is dormancy of spirits in fetishes RAW? I never played it like that- on the contrary, I treat fetish-bound spirits as pretty awake and in need of continued (albeit minor) chiminage. The moment a player treats a fetish like a mere object, the spirit would get annoyed. For example, the player with a Magpie's Swag regularly puts small glittery baubles into it for the spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, but I treated it differently than the Dormancy that happens when they are recovering. They have a vague feeling what's going on around them, more about impressions and emotions and they know if they are being treated right and used, as the Fetish itself is a temple to them, and unless their temple is keeping them happy they will be protesting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}